'''Badia Curta International Airport''' ({{lang|ca|Aeroport Internacional de Badia Curta}}; [[IATA airport code|IATA]]: BDC, [[ICAO airport code|ICAO]]: BDIB) is an international airport serving [[Badia Curta]], an industrial city in [[Jala Province]], [[Balboa]]. The airport is located on the [[Shendan Ocean]] coast and serves the industrial and petrochemical corridor of the Jala highlands. [[CIEA]], one of the world's largest integrated petroleum companies, maintains its principal refining operations at Badia Curta, and the airport handles significant business traveller traffic.

The airport handles both domestic and international traffic. [[Aeroístmus]] operates high-frequency services from both [[Sant Cristòfor International Airport|Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Cecilio Ríos International Airport|Sant Bart]], as well as a route to [[Portnou International Airport|Portnou]] and an international business service to [[Tanjung Seroja International Airport|Tanjung Seroja]]. [[RapidAir (Balboa)|RapidAir]] serves the airport from Sant Cristòfor. [[Okaiken Air]] operates international services to [[Okami-Tobu International Airport|Okami-Tobu]].

